<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The socket sorter ~ one class per proven presenter, before any verdict

A face gate proves a presenter first. Only then does it ask what class the presenter stands in, and it asks
ONE sorter, over the facts the gate itself read: the admit's verdict, the PersonaGroup grant, the fleet
shadow, the tier the gate stands at, and the posture of the one Nexus the gate stands in.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-four-classes`>>

!! Four classes, and silence

# ''same-operator'' — the gate read the admit HELD, the PersonaGroup ring answered a grant for this very
face, no fleet shadow sets the presenter's device aside, and the gate stands at the SOVEREIGN tier.
Same-operator establishes TRANSPORT alone: the session's proven face and its scoped document view decide
each document (house ruling "Sharing after the gate"; "A device set aside").
# ''contracted'' — the admit read HELD, standing as the proven face key at the admit's Nexus; or a faceless
PLACE presented a carriage contract the gate read HELD, standing as the place key.
# ''walker'' — SHUT by name (the shut-routes house ruling, stable-founding-road #/rulings): a grant or claim arm draws nothing until a
live grant reader opens the route (`SHUT_ARMS`). The shut arm's name goes to the
vessel's own log and never to the presenter.
# ''stranger'' — a proven presenter with no arm, answered only where THIS gate's Nexus reads OPEN.

A presenter that sorts nowhere meets SILENCE: no frame, no reason, the same end a failed proof meets.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-one-posture-reader`>>

!! The one posture reader ~ a lararium reads its charter, a herm answers the knock

`ownPlacePosture(placeClass, charter)` is the ONE reader of what a gate answers an arm-less proven peer
with.

* ''A LARARIUM reads its charter.'' OPEN only where the charter says so. An absent or torn charter reads
PRIVATE: for a hearth that is a fault, and a fault fails closed.
* ''A HERM ANSWERS THE KNOCK'' (operator ruling). A herm holds no charter by CLASS, a waystone and never a
broken lararium, so its absent charter is no fault to fail closed on: it answers ANY proven peer that
knocked. The knock is its silence: the path derives from the gate key, and only a peer handed that key can
knock at all (a bare route draws no upgrade). WHERE a herm stands a gate is the other half, read by
`herm-carriage`: only at a Nexus whose quorum counted its `carry`. A herm's SILENT or WAYMARK rung governs
its HTTP descriptor alone, never this.

One gate stands per (Nexus, route), so a sorter reads that Nexus's posture alone, fresh at every sort.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/a-refold-that-demotes-closes`>>

!! A refold that demotes closes

`socketsNoLongerHeld` names the admitted sessions a membership refold drops its hold on: a contracted
session whose admit the refolded membership does not read held, and every stranger (or classless) session
once the gate's Nexus stops answering strangers. Same-operator and walker sessions are never dropped here. The caller
drops each one the way the gate drops a refused one: no frame, no reason.

<<~/ahu>>

